{{ang-noun|f|byrġ}}

# [[city]] or [[town]]
#* '''c. 897''', [[w:Alfred the Great|King Alfred's]] [https://books.google.com/books?id=6JEtAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA162 translation] of [[w:Pope Gregory I|Pope Gregory's]] ''{{w|Pastoral Care}}''
#*: {{quote|ang|Wyrċaþ fæsten ymb þā '''burg'''.|Build a fortress around the '''city'''.}}
#* '''late 9th century''', [https://books.google.com/books?id=xtM0rOEXqJIC&pg=PA22 translation] of [[w:Orosius|Orosius’]] ''History Against the Pagans''
#*: {{quote|ang|Þæt Ēstland is swīðe miċel, and þǣr biþ swīðe manega '''byrġ''', and on ǣlcre '''byrġ''' biþ cyning.|Estonia is very large. There are a whole lot of '''towns''', and every '''town''' has a king.}}
#* '''late 9th century''', [[w:Alfred the Great|King Alfred's]] [https://books.google.com/books?id=qygPAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA69 translation] of [[w:Augustine of Hippo|St. Augustine's]] ''[[w:Soliloquies of Augustine|Soliloquies]]''
#*: {{quote|ang|Nāt iċ nā þȳ hwā Rōme '''burg''' timbrede þe iċ hit self ġesāwe, ac for þȳ þe hit man mē sæġde.|I don't know who built the '''city''' of Rome because I saw it myself, but because somebody told me.}}
#* '''c. 992''', [[w:Ælfric of Eynsham|Ælfric]], [https://books.google.com/books?id=2xobVW92JLcC&pg=PA450 "The Assumption of the Blessed Mary"]
#*: {{quote|ang|Sē Godes wiðersaca hine þā ġehāthierte and cwæþ, "Þā iċ fram fierde ġeċierre, iċ tōweorpe þās '''burg''', and hīe ġesmēðe, and tō ierþlande āwende, swā þæt hēo biþ cornbǣru swīðor þonne manbǣru."|The adversary of God became furious and said, "When I return from the campaign, I will destroy this '''city''', and level it, and turn it into farmland, so it is full of grain instead of people."}}
# [[fortified]] [[place]]: [[fortress]], [[castle]]
#* '''c. 897''', [[w:Alfred the Great|King Alfred's]] [https://books.google.com/books?id=6JEtAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA276 translation] of [[w:Pope Gregory I|Pope Gregory's]] ''{{w|Pastoral Care}}''
#*: {{quote|ang|Sēo '''burg''' þæs mōdes sċeal swīðe oft ġefrēdan hire fēonda speru.|The '''fortress''' of the mind must very often feel the spears of its enemies.}}
#* ''{{w|Anglo-Saxon Chronicle}}'', Manuscript A, [https://books.google.com/books?id=FvlsBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA360 year 921]
#*: {{quote|ang|Þā fōr Ēadweard cyning mid Westseaxna fierde tō Colneċeastre and ġebētte þā '''burg''' and ġeednīewode þǣr hēo ǣr tōbrocen wæs.|Then King Edward traveled to Colchester with the West Saxon army and repaired the '''fortress''', and rebuilt it where it had been destroyed.}}

